# The AIC8800D80 USB stick (368b:8d83) provides the BoatNetwork access point.
#
# The stick exposes three USB interfaces: two Bluetooth (class e0/01/01) and one
# vendor-specific Wi-Fi interface (ff/ff/ff) driven by aic8800_fdrv. Only the
# Wi-Fi is wanted. The Bluetooth radio creates a second controller, which BlueZ
# may pick as the default, and its address is generated (locally administered),
# so bonds stored against it cannot survive an address change.
#
# Deauthorising just those two interfaces stops btusb binding, so the second
# radio never appears at all. The Wi-Fi interface does not match this rule.
#
# A oneshot service that powers the radio off after boot was not enough: BlueZ
# powered it back on about 40 s later. Not existing is the only reliable state.
#
# Verify with:  busctl tree org.bluez --list | grep hci
#               nmcli -t -f NAME,DEVICE,STATE con show --active | grep BoatNetwork
#
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ENV{DEVTYPE}=="usb_interface", \
  ATTRS{idVendor}=="368b", ATTRS{idProduct}=="8d83", \
  ATTR{bInterfaceClass}=="e0", ATTR{authorized}="0"
